		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-07-07T20:02:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				143,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Maintain): Update Architecture.md and README.md for config-driven build profiles\n\nBoth documentation files had fallen out of sync with the actual codebase architecture. The CLI moved from flat `CLI.rs` files to `CLI/` directories with subcommands for `list-profiles`, `show-profile`, `validate-profile`, and `resolve`. The Rhai engine is no longer a user-facing scripting surface — it now exclusively backs the config-loader pipeline that reads `.vscode/land-config.json`. The `Eliminate` transform pipeline gained new files (`Inline/`, `CollectBlockPatches`, `PreservePass`, `TryBlockPreserve`, etc.) and the Run module similarly restructured.\n\n- Rewrite the Architecture.md narrative to describe config-driven profiles resolved from `land-config.json` as the primary build mechanism\n- Update all Mermaid diagram node paths (`CLI.rs` → `CLI/Cli.rs`, `Inline.rs` → `Inline/Eliminator.rs`)\n- Add `CreateEngine.rs`, `RegisterUtilityFunctions.rs`, and `Substitutor.rs` to the component table\n- Fix directory tree listing to match actual `Source/Build/CLI/`, `Source/Build/Process/`, `Source/Eliminate/Transform/Inline/`, `Source/Run/CLI/` structure\n- Bump minimum Rust version to 1.95.0+ (edition 2024) in README badges and prerequisites\n- Add `land-config.json` to Key Dependencies table; remove outdated `.rhai` scripting references\n- Normalize whitespace: replace literal emoji/whitespace sequences with `&#x2001;` Unicode en-space across both files\n- Add License, Changelog, and Project Maintainers sections to README\n\nBoth documents now accurately reflect the current codebase architecture.",
			"SHA": "cb4c55406459ba42ca362c119a6d0e39f305f5cb"
		},
